    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key to `SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))` and rewired duplicate detection around it, keeping structural impact low by concentrating the new logic in one small cohesive class rather than growing the large `Owner` and controller classes.\n\n**Changes (4 files):**\n\n1. **New `IdentityKey.java`** (model) \u2014 a self-contained utility holding all the new logic: `of(telephone, email, lastName)` produces the 64-char lowercase SHA-256 hex, and `soundex(lastName)` implements standard Soundex via a compact lookup table. Being a fresh, single-purpose class, its methods carry no surrounding-class complexity.\n\n2. **`Owner.getIdentityKey()`** \u2014 replaced the old `tel|email|` string with a one-line delegation to `IdentityKey.of(...)`. Minimal edit, CC=1, inside the large `Owner` class.\n\n3. **`PossibleDuplicate.matches()`** \u2014 the soft-match now triggers when the **identity key differs** but **soundex(lastName) and postcode match** (previously it keyed off exact last name + differing telephone). Small class, tiny edit.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner()`** \u2014 replaced the two hard-coded `setPossibleDuplicate(false)` lines with a 3-line wiring of `PossibleDuplicate.of(owner, owners)` (plus one import).\n\n**Behavioral effects delivered:**\n- Duplicate detection (409) now uses the single identity key, over the non-deleted owner set (blocklist still applied first via the unchanged `NonDisposableEmail` bean validation).\n- Two owners with the same last name and postcode but **different telephones** are no longer a hard 409 \u2014 telephone is part of the key, so they diverge and instead surface as a soft match.\n- The identity key is the sole duplicate check; there was no separate household-id 409 block, so nothing there needed removing \u2014 household id remains only for member counting/level capping.",
